 Housekeeping scripts for the CI workers.
 
-`bin/clean-workspaces.sh` removes stale build workspaces under `workspaces/`. The root and
-the age threshold are hardcoded, so a worker with a different layout needs its own copy of
-the script.
+`bin/clean-workspaces.sh` removes stale build workspaces: directories directly under the
+workspace root whose newest file is more than the threshold number of days old.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [-n|--dry-run] [-r|--root DIR] [-d|--days N]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` | Directory containing the workspaces. Must exist; `/` is refused. |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Remove workspaces older than `N` whole days (non-negative integer). |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | Print `would remove ...` for each stale workspace and remove nothing. |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage. |
+
+Symlinks under the root are never followed or removed, and a workspace containing no files is
+skipped with a warning. Exit status is 0 on success, 1 if a removal failed, 64 for bad
+arguments, and 66 if the root is missing.
+
+Preview before deleting, then run for real with a custom root and threshold:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --dry-run --root /var/ci/workspaces --days 3
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /var/ci/workspaces --days 3
+```
